IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg9-x-dissolution`

-- Tests of dg9-x-dissolution.l4 (8 Del. C. sections 273 to 277).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text, beside the assertion, before the run.
-- The wrappers `t ...` only give a rule's inputs short positional names; they restate no rule.

§ `Test wrappers`

GIVEN stateCorp IS A BOOLEAN
      holders IS A NUMBER
      mine IS A NUMBER
      theirs IS A NUMBER
      jv IS A BOOLEAN
      disagree IS A BOOLEAN
      certOther IS A BOOLEAN
      agreeOther IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t 273(a) may petition` stateCorp holders mine theirs jv disagree certOther agreeOther MEANS
    `s 273(a) either stockholder may file a petition with the Court of Chancery` WITH `the corporation is a corporation of this State` IS stateCorp, `the number of stockholders` IS holders, `the proportion of the stock owned by the petitioner` IS mine, `the proportion of the stock owned by the other stockholder` IS theirs, `the stockholders are engaged in the prosecution of a joint venture` IS jv, `the stockholders are unable to agree upon the desirability of discontinuing the joint venture and disposing of the assets used in it` IS disagree, `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` IS certOther, `a written agreement between the stockholders provides otherwise` IS agreeOther

GIVEN stated IS A BOOLEAN
      plan IS A BOOLEAN
      cert IS A BOOLEAN
      acknowledged IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t 273(a) petition in order` stated plan cert acknowledged MEANS
    `s 273(a) the petition is in order` WITH `the petition states that the stockholder desires to discontinue the joint venture and dispose of its assets in accordance with a plan to be agreed upon by both stockholders or, if no plan is agreed, that the corporation be dissolved` IS stated, `a copy of the proposed plan of discontinuance and distribution is attached` IS plan, `a certificate is attached stating that copies of the petition and plan have been transmitted in writing to the other stockholder and to the directors and officers` IS cert, `the petition and the certificate were executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103` IS acknowledged

GIVEN asOf IS A DATE
      lastDay1 IS A DATE
      lastDay2 IS A DATE
      first IS A BOOLEAN
      second IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t 273(b) court may dissolve` asOf lastDay1 lastDay2 first second MEANS
    `s 273(b) the Court of Chancery may dissolve the corporation and appoint trustees or receivers to administer and wind up its affairs` WITH `the date of the question` IS asOf, `the last day of the 3-month period, as extended` IS lastDay1, `the last day of the 1-year period, as extended` IS lastDay2, `the first certificate was filed within its period` IS first, `the second certificate was filed within its period` IS second

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 274 Certificate of surrender`
`t 274 certificate` a b c d e f MEANS
    `s 274 Certificate of surrender` WITH `statement that no shares have been issued or that the business has not been begun` IS a, `statement of the date of filing of the original certificate of incorporation` IS b, `statement that no part of the capital has been paid or that the amount paid in, less necessary expenses, has been returned` IS c, `statement that all debts of the corporation have been paid` IS d, `statement that all issued stock certificates have been surrendered and cancelled` IS e, `statement that all rights and franchises of the corporation are surrendered` IS f

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 275(d) Certificate of dissolution`
`t 275(d) certificate` a b c d e f MEANS
    `s 275(d) Certificate of dissolution` WITH `statement of the name of the corporation` IS a, `statement of the date dissolution was authorized` IS b, `statement that the dissolution was authorized by the board of directors and stockholders under subsections (a) and (b), or by all of the stockholders entitled to vote under subsection (c)` IS c, `statement of the names and addresses of the directors and officers` IS d, `statement of the date of filing of the original certificate of incorporation` IS e, `the agreement required by subsection (i)` IS f

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 275(f) Certificate of dissolution on expiry`
`t 275(f) certificate` a b c d e MEANS
    `s 275(f) Certificate of dissolution on expiry` WITH `statement of the name of the corporation` IS a, `statement of the date specified in the certificate of incorporation limiting the duration of the corporation's existence` IS b, `statement of the names and addresses of the directors and officers` IS c, `statement of the date of filing of the original certificate of incorporation` IS d, `the agreement required by subsection (i)` IS e

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
      g IS A BOOLEAN
      h IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 275(i) Record of service on the Secretary of State`
`t 275(i) record` a b c d e f g h MEANS
    `s 275(i) Record of service on the Secretary of State` WITH `entry of the name of the plaintiff` IS a, `entry of the name of the defendant` IS b, `entry of the title of the proceeding` IS c, `entry of the docket number` IS d, `entry of the nature of the proceeding` IS e, `entry of the fact that service has been effected pursuant to the subsection` IS f, `entry of the return date` IS g, `entry of the day and hour service was made` IS h

§ `s 273 Dissolution of joint venture corporation having 2 stockholders`

§§ `s 273(a) the petition`

-- The text's case: a Delaware corporation, 2 stockholders at 50% each, a joint venture, unable to agree, nothing in the certificate or a written agreement.
--  columns: Delaware, holders, mine, theirs, joint venture, unable to agree, certificate otherwise, agreement otherwise
#ASSERT `t 273(a) may petition` TRUE 2 (50%) (50%) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Not a corporation of this State.
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(a) may petition` FALSE 2 (50%) (50%) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Three stockholders (or one) are not "only 2 stockholders".
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(a) may petition` TRUE 3 (50%) (50%) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(a) may petition` TRUE 1 (50%) (50%) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- 51% and 49%: each must own 50%.
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(a) may petition` TRUE 2 (51%) (49%) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(a) may petition` TRUE 2 (49%) (51%) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- No joint venture; able to agree.
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(a) may petition` TRUE 2 (50%) (50%) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(a) may petition` TRUE 2 (50%) (50%) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- "unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation ... or in a written agreement between the stockholders".
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(a) may petition` TRUE 2 (50%) (50%) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(a) may petition` TRUE 2 (50%) (50%) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- The petition is in order only with the statement, the plan, the certificate and the section 103 execution.
--  columns: stated, plan attached, certificate attached, executed and acknowledged under section 103
#ASSERT `t 273(a) petition in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(a) petition in order` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(a) petition in order` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(a) petition in order` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(a) petition in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§§ `s 273(b) the periods and the Court's power`

-- Petition filed 15 January 2026: 3 months ends 15 April 2026, 1 year ends 15 January 2027.
#ASSERT (`s 273(b) the last day of a period, as extended` WITH `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 1 15, `the period` IS `period in months` 3, `the extension the stockholders agreed, if any` IS NOTHING) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 15
#ASSERT (`s 273(b) the last day of a period, as extended` WITH `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 1 15, `the period` IS `period in years` 1, `the extension the stockholders agreed, if any` IS NOTHING) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 1 15
-- Months clamp to the last day of the month (the core's reading, fork F2 of the core): 30 November plus 3 months is 28 February.
#ASSERT (`s 273(b) the last day of a period, as extended` WITH `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 11 30, `the period` IS `period in months` 3, `the extension the stockholders agreed, if any` IS NOTHING) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 2 28
-- An extension to 15 July 2026, certificate filed on the last day (15 April): "prior to the expiration" holds, the period is extended.
#ASSERT (`s 273(b) the last day of a period, as extended` WITH `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 1 15, `the period` IS `period in months` 3, `the extension the stockholders agreed, if any` IS JUST (`s 273(b) Extension of a period` WITH `the date to which the period is extended` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 15, `the date the certificate of extension was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 15)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 7 15
-- The certificate of extension filed the day after the last day is too late: the period is not extended.
#ASSERT (`s 273(b) the last day of a period, as extended` WITH `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 1 15, `the period` IS `period in months` 3, `the extension the stockholders agreed, if any` IS JUST (`s 273(b) Extension of a period` WITH `the date to which the period is extended` IS YearMonthDay 2026 7 15, `the date the certificate of extension was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 16)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 15
-- An "extension" to an earlier date does not shorten the period.
#ASSERT (`s 273(b) the last day of a period, as extended` WITH `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 1 15, `the period` IS `period in months` 3, `the extension the stockholders agreed, if any` IS JUST (`s 273(b) Extension of a period` WITH `the date to which the period is extended` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 1, `the date the certificate of extension was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 15

-- The stockholders' certificate is filed in time on the last day, not the day after, and not at all is not in time.
#ASSERT `s 273(b) the stockholders' certificate was filed within the period` WITH `the date both stockholders filed the certificate with the Court of Chancery, if they did` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 15), `the last day of the period, as extended` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 15
#ASSERT NOT (`s 273(b) the stockholders' certificate was filed within the period` WITH `the date both stockholders filed the certificate with the Court of Chancery, if they did` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 16), `the last day of the period, as extended` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 273(b) the stockholders' certificate was filed within the period` WITH `the date both stockholders filed the certificate with the Court of Chancery, if they did` IS NOTHING, `the last day of the period, as extended` IS YearMonthDay 2026 4 15)

-- Both certificates filed in time: the Court has no power under subsection (b), however late the date.
--  columns: date of the question, last day of period 1, last day of period 2, first filed in time, second filed in time
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(b) court may dissolve` (YearMonthDay 2027 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 15) TRUE TRUE)
-- The first certificate was not filed and the 3-month period has run out (16 April): the Court may dissolve.
#ASSERT `t 273(b) court may dissolve` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 16) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 15) FALSE FALSE
-- On the last day itself (15 April) the period has not yet failed.
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(b) court may dissolve` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 15) FALSE FALSE)
-- The first filed, the second not, the year has run out (16 January 2027): the Court may dissolve (either failure is enough).
#ASSERT `t 273(b) court may dissolve` (YearMonthDay 2027 1 16) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 15) TRUE FALSE
-- The same, but the year has not run out (1 June 2026): not yet.
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(b) court may dissolve` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 15) TRUE FALSE)
-- Neither filed, both periods run out.
#ASSERT `t 273(b) court may dissolve` (YearMonthDay 2027 1 16) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 15) FALSE FALSE
-- On the last day of the year (15 January 2027) the second period has not yet failed.
#ASSERT NOT (`t 273(b) court may dissolve` (YearMonthDay 2027 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 15) TRUE FALSE)

§§ `s 273(c) the Attorney General`

-- Charitable nonstock corporation, petition filed 1 May 2026: a copy to the Attorney General within 1 week, so by 8 May.
#ASSERT `s 273(c) the petitioner has complied with the duty to provide a copy of the petition to the Attorney General` WITH `the kind of corporation` IS `a charitable nonstock corporation`, `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the date the petitioner gave the Attorney General a copy of the petition, if the petitioner did` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 8)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 273(c) the petitioner has complied with the duty to provide a copy of the petition to the Attorney General` WITH `the kind of corporation` IS `a charitable nonstock corporation`, `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the date the petitioner gave the Attorney General a copy of the petition, if the petitioner did` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 9))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 273(c) the petitioner has complied with the duty to provide a copy of the petition to the Attorney General` WITH `the kind of corporation` IS `a charitable nonstock corporation`, `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the date the petitioner gave the Attorney General a copy of the petition, if the petitioner did` IS NOTHING)
-- Any other kind of corporation: no such duty, so nothing to comply with.
#ASSERT `s 273(c) the petitioner has complied with the duty to provide a copy of the petition to the Attorney General` WITH `the kind of corporation` IS `a stock corporation`, `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the date the petitioner gave the Attorney General a copy of the petition, if the petitioner did` IS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 273(c) the petitioner has complied with the duty to provide a copy of the petition to the Attorney General` WITH `the kind of corporation` IS `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable`, `the date the petition was filed with the Court of Chancery` IS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, `the date the petitioner gave the Attorney General a copy of the petition, if the petitioner did` IS NOTHING

§ `s 274 Dissolution before issuance of shares or beginning of business`

-- "has not issued shares or has not commenced the business": either is enough.
#ASSERT `s 274 the corporation has not issued shares or has not commenced business` WITH `the corporation has issued shares` IS FALSE, `the corporation has commenced the business for which it was organized` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 274 the corporation has not issued shares or has not commenced business` WITH `the corporation has issued shares` IS FALSE, `the corporation has commenced the business for which it was organized` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 274 the corporation has not issued shares or has not commenced business` WITH `the corporation has issued shares` IS TRUE, `the corporation has commenced the business for which it was organized` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 274 the corporation has not issued shares or has not commenced business` WITH `the corporation has issued shares` IS TRUE, `the corporation has commenced the business for which it was organized` IS TRUE)

-- Directors named or elected: a majority of the directors. 5 directors: 3 is a majority, 2 is not.
#ASSERT (`s 274 a majority of the incorporators, or of the directors, may surrender the rights and franchises` WITH `directors were named in the certificate of incorporation or have been elected` IS TRUE, `the number of incorporators` IS 3, `the number of directors` IS 5, `the number of those who execute and acknowledge the certificate` IS 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 274 a majority of the incorporators, or of the directors, may surrender the rights and franchises` WITH `directors were named in the certificate of incorporation or have been elected` IS TRUE, `the number of incorporators` IS 3, `the number of directors` IS 5, `the number of those who execute and acknowledge the certificate` IS 2) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 4 directors: 2 is exactly half, not a majority; 3 is.
#ASSERT (`s 274 a majority of the incorporators, or of the directors, may surrender the rights and franchises` WITH `directors were named in the certificate of incorporation or have been elected` IS TRUE, `the number of incorporators` IS 3, `the number of directors` IS 4, `the number of those who execute and acknowledge the certificate` IS 2) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 274 a majority of the incorporators, or of the directors, may surrender the rights and franchises` WITH `directors were named in the certificate of incorporation or have been elected` IS TRUE, `the number of incorporators` IS 3, `the number of directors` IS 4, `the number of those who execute and acknowledge the certificate` IS 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No directors named or elected: a majority of the incorporators. 3 incorporators: 2 is a majority, 1 is not.
#ASSERT (`s 274 a majority of the incorporators, or of the directors, may surrender the rights and franchises` WITH `directors were named in the certificate of incorporation or have been elected` IS FALSE, `the number of incorporators` IS 3, `the number of directors` IS 0, `the number of those who execute and acknowledge the certificate` IS 2) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 274 a majority of the incorporators, or of the directors, may surrender the rights and franchises` WITH `directors were named in the certificate of incorporation or have been elected` IS FALSE, `the number of incorporators` IS 3, `the number of directors` IS 0, `the number of those who execute and acknowledge the certificate` IS 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: more signatories than there are directors, or no incorporators at all.
#ASSERT (`s 274 a majority of the incorporators, or of the directors, may surrender the rights and franchises` WITH `directors were named in the certificate of incorporation or have been elected` IS TRUE, `the number of incorporators` IS 3, `the number of directors` IS 5, `the number of those who execute and acknowledge the certificate` IS 6) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 274 a majority of the incorporators, or of the directors, may surrender the rights and franchises` WITH `directors were named in the certificate of incorporation or have been elected` IS FALSE, `the number of incorporators` IS 0, `the number of directors` IS 0, `the number of those who execute and acknowledge the certificate` IS 0) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The certificate of surrender: all the statements; the debts statement only where business began without shares issued; the surrender of certificates only where business has not begun but stock certificates were issued.
--  columns of the certificate: no shares/business not begun, date of original certificate, capital returned, debts paid, stock certificates surrendered, rights and franchises surrendered
#ASSERT `s 274 the certificate of surrender states what the section requires` WITH `the certificate` IS (`t 274 certificate` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE), `the corporation has begun business but has not issued shares` IS FALSE, `the corporation has not begun business but has issued stock certificates` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 274 the certificate of surrender states what the section requires` WITH `the certificate` IS (`t 274 certificate` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE), `the corporation has begun business but has not issued shares` IS FALSE, `the corporation has not begun business but has issued stock certificates` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 274 the certificate of surrender states what the section requires` WITH `the certificate` IS (`t 274 certificate` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE), `the corporation has begun business but has not issued shares` IS FALSE, `the corporation has not begun business but has issued stock certificates` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 274 the certificate of surrender states what the section requires` WITH `the certificate` IS (`t 274 certificate` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE), `the corporation has begun business but has not issued shares` IS FALSE, `the corporation has not begun business but has issued stock certificates` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 274 the certificate of surrender states what the section requires` WITH `the certificate` IS (`t 274 certificate` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE), `the corporation has begun business but has not issued shares` IS FALSE, `the corporation has not begun business but has issued stock certificates` IS FALSE)
-- Business begun, no shares issued: the debts statement is required.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 274 the certificate of surrender states what the section requires` WITH `the certificate` IS (`t 274 certificate` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE), `the corporation has begun business but has not issued shares` IS TRUE, `the corporation has not begun business but has issued stock certificates` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 274 the certificate of surrender states what the section requires` WITH `the certificate` IS (`t 274 certificate` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE), `the corporation has begun business but has not issued shares` IS TRUE, `the corporation has not begun business but has issued stock certificates` IS FALSE
-- Business not begun but stock certificates issued: their surrender is required.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 274 the certificate of surrender states what the section requires` WITH `the certificate` IS (`t 274 certificate` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE), `the corporation has begun business but has not issued shares` IS FALSE, `the corporation has not begun business but has issued stock certificates` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 274 the certificate of surrender states what the section requires` WITH `the certificate` IS (`t 274 certificate` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE), `the corporation has begun business but has not issued shares` IS FALSE, `the corporation has not begun business but has issued stock certificates` IS TRUE
-- "Upon such certificate becoming effective in accordance with § 103 ... the corporation shall be dissolved."
#ASSERT `s 274 the corporation is dissolved by the certificate of surrender` WITH `the certificate has become effective in accordance with § 103` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 274 the corporation is dissolved by the certificate of surrender` WITH `the certificate has become effective in accordance with § 103` IS FALSE)

§ `s 275 Dissolution generally; procedure`

§§ `s 275(a) to (c) authorization`

-- A majority of the whole board: 5 of 9 and 5 of 8 are majorities; 4 of 8 is exactly half; 0 of 0 and 10 of 9 are not counts.
#ASSERT (`s 275(a) the board adopted the resolution to dissolve by a majority of the whole board` WITH `the number of directors who voted for the resolution` IS 5, `the number of directors constituting the whole board` IS 9) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 275(a) the board adopted the resolution to dissolve by a majority of the whole board` WITH `the number of directors who voted for the resolution` IS 5, `the number of directors constituting the whole board` IS 8) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 275(a) the board adopted the resolution to dissolve by a majority of the whole board` WITH `the number of directors who voted for the resolution` IS 4, `the number of directors constituting the whole board` IS 8) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 275(a) the board adopted the resolution to dissolve by a majority of the whole board` WITH `the number of directors who voted for the resolution` IS 0, `the number of directors constituting the whole board` IS 0) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 275(a) the board adopted the resolution to dissolve by a majority of the whole board` WITH `the number of directors who voted for the resolution` IS 10, `the number of directors constituting the whole board` IS 9) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The meeting was called for that purpose and each stockholder entitled to vote was given notice.
#ASSERT `s 275(a) the board has done what the subsection requires before the stockholders vote` WITH `the meeting of the board was called for the purpose of the resolution` IS TRUE, `notice of the adoption of the resolution and of the meeting of stockholders was given to each stockholder entitled to vote as of the record date` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 275(a) the board has done what the subsection requires before the stockholders vote` WITH `the meeting of the board was called for the purpose of the resolution` IS FALSE, `notice of the adoption of the resolution and of the meeting of stockholders was given to each stockholder entitled to vote as of the record date` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 275(a) the board has done what the subsection requires before the stockholders vote` WITH `the meeting of the board was called for the purpose of the resolution` IS TRUE, `notice of the adoption of the resolution and of the meeting of stockholders was given to each stockholder entitled to vote as of the record date` IS FALSE)
-- (b): a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote.
#ASSERT (`s 275(b) a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote has voted for the proposed dissolution` WITH `the votes for the proposed dissolution` IS 51, `the votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote thereon` IS 100) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 275(b) a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote has voted for the proposed dissolution` WITH `the votes for the proposed dissolution` IS 50, `the votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote thereon` IS 100) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 275(b) a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote has voted for the proposed dissolution` WITH `the votes for the proposed dissolution` IS 101, `the votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote thereon` IS 100) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c): all the stockholders entitled to vote consent in writing: 10 of 10, not 9 of 10.
#ASSERT (`s 275(c) all the stockholders entitled to vote have consented in writing to the dissolution` WITH `the number of stockholders entitled to vote who consented in writing` IS 10, `the number of stockholders entitled to vote` IS 10) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 275(c) all the stockholders entitled to vote have consented in writing to the dissolution` WITH `the number of stockholders entitled to vote who consented in writing` IS 9, `the number of stockholders entitled to vote` IS 10) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 275(c) all the stockholders entitled to vote have consented in writing to the dissolution` WITH `the number of stockholders entitled to vote who consented in writing` IS 0, `the number of stockholders entitled to vote` IS 0) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Authorized by either route.
--  inputs: board resolution (maybe), board did what s 275(a) requires, stockholders' vote (maybe), unanimous consent (maybe)
#ASSERT (`s 275 the dissolution is authorized in accordance with this section` WITH `the resolution of the board was adopted by a majority of the whole board` IS NOTHING, `the board did what s 275(a) requires before the stockholders voted` IS FALSE, `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote voted for the proposed dissolution` IS NOTHING, `all the stockholders entitled to vote consented in writing` IS JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 275 the dissolution is authorized in accordance with this section` WITH `the resolution of the board was adopted by a majority of the whole board` IS JUST TRUE, `the board did what s 275(a) requires before the stockholders voted` IS TRUE, `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote voted for the proposed dissolution` IS JUST TRUE, `all the stockholders entitled to vote consented in writing` IS JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 275 the dissolution is authorized in accordance with this section` WITH `the resolution of the board was adopted by a majority of the whole board` IS JUST TRUE, `the board did what s 275(a) requires before the stockholders voted` IS TRUE, `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote voted for the proposed dissolution` IS JUST TRUE, `all the stockholders entitled to vote consented in writing` IS NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The board's resolution failed: not authorized.
#ASSERT (`s 275 the dissolution is authorized in accordance with this section` WITH `the resolution of the board was adopted by a majority of the whole board` IS JUST FALSE, `the board did what s 275(a) requires before the stockholders voted` IS TRUE, `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote voted for the proposed dissolution` IS JUST TRUE, `all the stockholders entitled to vote consented in writing` IS JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The stockholders' vote failed: not authorized.
#ASSERT (`s 275 the dissolution is authorized in accordance with this section` WITH `the resolution of the board was adopted by a majority of the whole board` IS JUST TRUE, `the board did what s 275(a) requires before the stockholders voted` IS TRUE, `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote voted for the proposed dissolution` IS JUST FALSE, `all the stockholders entitled to vote consented in writing` IS JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The board did not call the meeting for that purpose or give notice: not authorized.
#ASSERT (`s 275 the dissolution is authorized in accordance with this section` WITH `the resolution of the board was adopted by a majority of the whole board` IS JUST TRUE, `the board did what s 275(a) requires before the stockholders voted` IS FALSE, `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote voted for the proposed dissolution` IS JUST TRUE, `all the stockholders entitled to vote consented in writing` IS JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: the board's count cannot be a vote and there was no unanimous consent.
#ASSERT (`s 275 the dissolution is authorized in accordance with this section` WITH `the resolution of the board was adopted by a majority of the whole board` IS NOTHING, `the board did what s 275(a) requires before the stockholders voted` IS TRUE, `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote voted for the proposed dissolution` IS JUST TRUE, `all the stockholders entitled to vote consented in writing` IS JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 275 the dissolution is authorized in accordance with this section` WITH `the resolution of the board was adopted by a majority of the whole board` IS JUST TRUE, `the board did what s 275(a) requires before the stockholders voted` IS TRUE, `a majority of the outstanding stock entitled to vote voted for the proposed dissolution` IS NOTHING, `all the stockholders entitled to vote consented in writing` IS JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 275(d) the certificate of dissolution`

--  columns: name, date authorized, route statement, names and addresses of directors and officers, date of original certificate, the agreement under (i)
#ASSERT `s 275(d) the certificate of dissolution is in order` WITH `the certificate` IS (`t 275(d) certificate` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE), `the certificate was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 275(d) the certificate of dissolution is in order` WITH `the certificate` IS (`t 275(d) certificate` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE), `the certificate was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103` IS TRUE)
